    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d338">

                <pb facs="0766" n="740" xml:id="pg740"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Eisenhower Library, Dulles papers, “Telephone
                    Conversations”</note>
                <head>No. 338<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Telephone Conversations, by
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            type="conversation-or-meeting-date" when="1953-07-28T09:08:00-04:00"
                            >July 28, 1953—9:08 a.m. and 10:10 a.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Telephone Conversations With
                        Allen W. Dulles—Iran</hi></p>
                <p>The Secretary telephoned his brother and asked if he wanted to bring this up at
                    press conference.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d338-f1"/> AWD said he worked yesterday
                    with State people on a draft. It has his enthusiastic approval as well as those
                    on the other end.</p>
                <p>The Secretary called him again and said the people here were not willing to go
                    quite as far—do they know about this? Yes, Jernegan and Byroade both know about
                    it.</p>
                <p>The Secretary called his brother again about the wording of the statement “any
                    further aid to Iran”, what did it mean, increase or threat to cut it off
                    entirely? AWD said that was the point of using the word, the Secretary thought
                    it would be more tricky when translated, AWD defers to his judgment in the light
                    of the Eisenhower letter.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d338-f1" n="1" xml:id="d338-f1-content">
                <p>Presumably a reference to Secretary Dulles’ statement made later that day at a
                    press conference; see <ref target="#d339"><hi rendition="#italic"
                        >infra</hi></ref>.</p>
            </note>
